  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Philippines Emergency Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Philipinas and Community Organizers&apos; Multiversity (COM) propose a 6 -month humanitarian response to address the unmet needs of 15,250 of the most vulnerable, hard -to -reach Indigenous People (IP) community members in Geographically Isolated and Disadvantaged Areas (GIDA) areas of San Gabriel and Santol, as well as in coastal communities in Luna and Santo Tomas. Oxfam and COM will implement an integrated response across four sectors: Food Security through multipurpose cash assistance and top -up cash for food and essential Non Food Items (NFIs); Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) through water access restoration, sanitation repairs, and hygiene promotion; Protection, including Gender Based Violence (GBV) referrals and psychosocial support; and Gender Inclusion through awareness, assistance, and support for unpaid care work.</narrative>
  </description>
